    m_Localized: Come back anytime to continue restoring the artifact.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 626313739505664
    m_Localized: Are you sure you want to start a new game?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 626544380088320
    m_Localized: Your progress will be reset and cannot be recovered.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 626889151877120
    m_Localized: Confirm
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 632810972254208
    m_Localized: Language
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661625995923456
    m_Localized: Coin inscribed Chong Ning Tong Bao
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661675153166336
    m_Localized: "The characters on this coin exhibit Emperor Huizong\u2019s distinctive
      calligraphic style, known as \u201Cslender gold\u201D because it resembled
      finely spun filaments of the precious metal. Huizong made an effort to present
      himself as a man of cultivated tastes through various means. His writings were
      often carved in stone or metal, as here, and circulated widely among the public."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661711144488960
    m_Localized: "Hello, Nova. Welcome to the museum! We\u2019re delighted to have
      you here. I hope you\u2019ll have a wonderful time here!\n\n-Ms. Maya :)"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661745072214016
    m_Localized: "P.S Amazing to see this project in the hands of someone so competent!\nHeard
      from your Mama that you\u2019re happy to be here. Please send my hello to her.
      It\u2019s been a while since I\u2019ve worked with her."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661833643331584
    m_Localized: Paperweight in the shape of a horse
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661993203044352
    m_Localized: "Cast in silver, this elegant standing horse may have served as
      a paperweight on a scholar\u2019s desk. The figure reflects both the refined
      metalwork and cultivated aesthetics valued by intellectuals of the period."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662160123760640
    m_Localized: "Here\u2019s another Chinese artifact! A beauty... Something I would
      personally have in my house, to be honest :)\n\n- Ms. Maya"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662186422046720
    m_Localized: "p.s So your mom is Tara Arkana? I\u2019ve heard of her from an
      excavation project back in the early 2000s... Her dedication to represent Indonesia
      internationally was so inspiring for me as a young historian back then!\n\n-
      Ms. Maya"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662376306577408
    m_Localized: Jar with Dragon
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662389711572992
    m_Localized: White porcelain painted with cobalt blue, a style that first flourished
      in China in the fourteenth century, is arguably the most important development
      in the history of ceramics. Commissioned by the court, this spectacular storage
      jar, made in the kilns in Jingdezhen, is dated to the rule of the Xuande emperor
      by an inscription on its shoulder. Its painted decoration features an animated
      dragon undulating across a sparsely clouded sky.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662411404513280
    m_Localized: "A big artifact today! If I remember correctly, she should be out
      of hospital now, isn\u2019t she? I hope she\u2019ll have good recovery time
      at home."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662432128569344
    m_Localized: "And here\u2019s your artifact for today! a beautiful jar, I believe,
      it just needs good care. I know you can restore this one too, like everything
      you\u2019ve successfully restored before.\n\n-Ms. Maya"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662504727777280
    m_Localized: Kendi
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662559601856512
    m_Localized: Kendi is a traditional water container often used for storing and
      drinking water. They may also serve ritual and ceremonial purposes. The term
      is derived from the Sanskrit word "kundika," which refers to a water vessel.
      This kendi is made from gold, dated from 8-9th century Central Javanese period
      in Indonesia.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662600655704064
    m_Localized: "Here\u2019s your next artifact, Nova. Another Indonesian one! Also,
      thanks for connecting me with your Mama again. I called her yesterday. Glad
      to hear she\u2019s doing better!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662615998468096
    m_Localized: "Do you know when she\u2019ll get out from hospital? We got carried
      away talking yesterday and I forgot to ask her that.\n\n-Ms. Maya"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662704598945792
    m_Localized: Kris
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662738652499968
    m_Localized: The kris, with its sinuous, snakelike blade, is the most characteristic
      weapon of Indonesia. Considered from early times to be imbued with great spiritual
      power, it is still an integral part of Indonesian culture.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662756914499584
    m_Localized: "Good morning, Nova. I heard about your Mama. I\u2019m sorry I can\u2019t
      talk to you face to face today, but I hope she will be better soon!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662772081102848
    m_Localized: "Here\u2019s the Kris for today\u2019s artifact. Reminds me of a
      big discovery she did several years ago... Would you want to take a picture
      and maybe send it to her? Might cheer her up!\n\n-Ms. Maya"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662827815014400
    m_Localized: Winged Scarab Amulet
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662876884176896
    m_Localized: 'This winged scarab consists of three pieces: an actual scarab beetle
      and two separately made wings. The wings are not those of a beetle, but those
      of a bird, as is apparent by their shape and the indication of individual feathers.
      Each piece features several small holes that were used to fasten the winged
      scarab to the wrappings of a mummy. Winged scarabs, meant to guarantee the
      rebirth of the deceased, were very popular funerary amulets.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662906575654912
    m_Localized: Nice chat we had yesterday, Nova! Happy to know your Auntie is there
      to help your Mama.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 662950208999424
    m_Localized: "Here\u2019s a scarab amulet, one I personally think is exceptionally
      stunning. Were you an ancient Egypt nerd like I was in my teenage years?\n\n-Ms.
      Maya"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 670290119364608
    m_Localized: Replay
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 670376157122560
    m_Localized: Continue Story
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 671280864301056
    m_Localized: Peel off the sticky note...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 671435663478784
    m_Localized: Open the box and start restore...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681396854460416
    m_Localized: Just started my first day here and got a coin from China. Reminded
      me of my earliest memory with artefacts.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681702430478336
    m_Localized: "The artifact this time is a horse-shaped paperweight. I agree with
      Ms. Maya, this is something I would love to have at home :D\n\nAnyways, I chatted
      a little about Mama with Ms. Maya and found out that she is THAT famous in
      the Indonesian history scene...? I keep feeling prouder and prouder of her.
      I\u2019ll tell her that when I call tonight :) Hope that can help her feel
      better."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681728636489728
    m_Localized: What a beautiful artifact today! Working on this jar make me reflect
      on what me and Mama went through. Before this, I genuinely thought that our
      relationship was beyond repair.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681751302508544
    m_Localized: 'Another Indonesian artifact today: a golden Kendi. Reminded me
      of our recent (and first!) professional project together, handling incoming
      Indonesian artifacts.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681772164976640
    m_Localized: Restored a Kris today, had mixed feelings about it. When we went
      to Indonesia twenty years ago, Mama promised me to go to a carnival at the
      end of the project to celebrate my 8th birthday.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 681785788076032
    m_Localized: "A scarab amulet! So funny that Ms. Maya is an ancient Egypt nerd
      when she was younger... Reminds me of my ancient civilization nerd phase. Being
      the loner I was, I didn\u2019t have friends in high school. Mama was as busy
      as always and never really had time for me either."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 684852990316544
    m_Localized: 'To-do List:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 689846674132992
    m_Localized: Remove Dust
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 689932682530816
    m_Localized: Scrub Off Mud
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 690033010282496
    m_Localized: Reassembling Artifacts
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 690839084208128
    m_Localized: to zoom in/out
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 690751289036800
    m_Localized: Scroll
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 690784596004864
    m_Localized: Hold
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 691354648055808
    m_Localized: to grab & cleaning
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 691615315660800
    m_Localized: to rotate artifact
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 692064299126784
    m_Localized: Wrap Up
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 692417103007744
    m_Localized: ~ Restoration Complete ~
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 693192948584448
    m_Localized: Paused
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 693439103897600
    m_Localized: Resume
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 693643894984704
    m_Localized: Back to Main Menu
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 694035294851072
    m_Localized: Are you sure you want to exit?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 694091263643648
    m_Localized: You progress will not be saved and the game starts  from the beginning
      again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 698589835038720
    m_Localized: Unboxing Artefact...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 698550941257728
    m_Localized: Returning to Menu...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 698510105513984
    m_Localized: Displaying Artefact...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 720976676786176
    m_Localized: Drag artefact to the center for inspection.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 721210291130368
    m_Localized: Use the mouse wheel to Zoom in/out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 721439744724992
    m_Localized: Hold right click and rotate the mouse around to rotate the Coin.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 721534246588416
    m_Localized: Select the brush, then hold and drag across the artifact to clean
      it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 721780603228160
    m_Localized: Select the chisel, then tap the dirt repeatedly to remove it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 721970382901248
    m_Localized: Press "Tab" to find the remaining dust.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 722153502019584
    m_Localized: Press "Tab" to find the remaining dust.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 722369328320512
    m_Localized: "Nice work. The artifact is ready for display in the museum.\\nYou
      can tap <b>Wrap Up</b> in the bottom-right to finish, or keep restoring until
      it\u2019s perfect."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2027892690116608
    m_Localized: You can assemble all the pieces by dragging the correct part to
      the current inspected artifact
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2027892694310912
    m_Localized: You can detach the part by hold the left button to the part. But
      you need to return your tool first!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9730903877488640
    m_Localized: Pause
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9752920672571392
    m_Localized: Hint On
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9753015136686080
    m_Localized: Hint Off
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11897090187071488
    m_Localized: Drag
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11897175025258496
    m_Localized: Pinch
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11897869581029376
    m_Localized: to zoom or rotate
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11897974782562304
    m_Localized: to use tools & move artifact
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11898174888611840
    m_Localized: Artifact to separate pieces
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11917221072080896
    m_Localized: Pinch the artifact with two fingers to zoom in or out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11917584206532608
    m_Localized: Drag with two fingers to rotate the artifact.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11917800712310784
    m_Localized: Drag the Brush from the bottom-right corner, then move it across
      the artifact to remove the dust.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11918021454336000
    m_Localized: Drag the Chisel from the bottom-right corner, then move it across
      the artifact to remove the mud.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11919552463376384
    m_Localized: Hint Mode is now unlocked. Tap the toggle button in the top-right
      corner\nto switch to UV View and spot hidden dust more easily.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11919685057908736
    m_Localized: Hint Mode is now unlocked. Tap the toggle button in the top-right
      corner\nto switch to UV View and spot hidden dust more easily.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11919898854166528
    m_Localized: "Nice work. The artifact is ready for display in the museum.\\nYou
      can tap <b>Wrap Up</b> in the top-right to finish, or keep restoring until
      it\u2019s perfect."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11920289440337920
    m_Localized: Drag each piece to the correct spot to assemble the artifact.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11921232164687872
    m_Localized: Hold a piece to detach it from the artifact.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27490745039851520
    m_Localized: I was a tiny toddler obsessed with playing as a cashier. Mama was
      well on her way to the peak of her archeologist career and just got back from
      an excavation in China.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27490861284986880
    m_Localized: She showed me ancient coins in her office, how they were so convenient
      to carry around with strings (with those holes in the middle!).
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27490904515678208
    m_Localized: I was so fascinated by how cool that was compared to the modern
      coins I knew!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27490971410632704
    m_Localized: Anyways, Mama is still in the hospital.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27491019536076800
    m_Localized: "Good thing Mama has Auntie to stay with her. I hope she\u2019ll
      feel better soon, I\u2019ll call her as soon as I get home later."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522868757008384
    m_Localized: To more birthdays (and everything else) together with Mama!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522837022904320
    m_Localized: "That is very sweet of her. I still do love carnivals. But what
      I love more is that I\u2019m going with Mama this time for my birthday after
      a looong time!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522797873270784
    m_Localized: She told me she spent her time on the hospital bed looking for the
      best carnival available on my birthday!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522765396774912
    m_Localized: Anyways, I need to go now. Mama got out from the hospital yesterday
      and she told me she got tickets for a carnival on my birthday next week.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522740243533824
    m_Localized: "I don\u2019t know if I have fully forgiven her. Wounds don\u2019t
      heal in an instant. But I\u2019m glad that Mama is doing her part of acknowledging
      her mistakes and trying to make it up by being there for me whenever she can
      now. \n\nI\u2019m doing my part too, of actively trying to forgive her and
      slowly building a good relationship with her. After all, I still love her."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522703207829504
    m_Localized: "After the outburst I had that day, Mama apologized over and over
      saying that it is fully her fault, and in her mind, she was just trying to
      make ends meet to provide for us. But she said that wasn\u2019t an excuse and
      she should have done better to be there for me, her only child."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522678234943488
    m_Localized: "I guess it turns out that there\u2019s lots of things that can
      be fixed with lots of patience, care, and willingness to work on it together."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522344007634944
    m_Localized: The rest of the night was filled with sobbing, hugging, apologizing,
      and possibly, the start of forgiving.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522297438277632
    m_Localized: Every important milestone in my life was filled with empty promises.
      Mama stayed silent the whole time, listening to every word. When I was finished,
      she simply walked over to me in tears, hugged me, and told me that she is truly
      sorry.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522269298692096
    m_Localized: All the resentment that has built up my whole life opened like floodgates
      and I told her exactly how she has abandoned me for work over and over again
      my whole entire life.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522234909593600
    m_Localized: "That was the tipping point for me. How dare she ask that? She made
      me feel like I was a stranger in her house. I couldn\u2019t hold it in."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522194082238464
    m_Localized: Why do you act like a stranger in the house? Why do you never eat
      when I cook you something?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522162889199616
    m_Localized: However, at the end of the project, we were having a closing dinner
      when Mama suddenly asked,
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522134237908992
    m_Localized: During this project we spent lots of time working closely and had
      our meals together. I think we are both slowly warming up to each other again
      after practically being roommates in the house for so long.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27522110653337600
    m_Localized: "Isn\u2019t it crazy that this is the most time we spent together
      in a last decade?"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27521887495393280
    m_Localized: "Funny how I found comfort and purpose in the same field that made
      Mama never have time for me. I think it\u2019s on this period that I made the
      love of history my own instead of something that\u2019s simply passed down
      from Mama. \n\nLovely how this love eventually made it all the way to going
      to college for history and conservation!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27521792188223488
    m_Localized: "It was so, so interesting and before I knew it, I was devouring
      every single one of Mama\u2019s history books."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27521756834435072
    m_Localized: "Now that I look back, I sure was a gloomy, quiet teen. I had to
      figure out what to do with all this time alone. On one fateful day, out of
      boredom, I picked up one of Mama\u2019s ancient civilization book off the shelf."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27521550529204224
    m_Localized: "Something more important always comes up and I\u2019m left alone
      again. My resentment for her grew over time. Consequently, I got used to being
      alone all the time. I felt like being alone felt safer than clinging on false
      hope for a company that never came."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27521508632301568
    m_Localized: "This wasn\u2019t the first time nor the last time. On so many other
      important events in my life (my birthdays, winning competitions, my first heartbreak)
      she always promised to be there for me but never kept her promise."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27521481209942016
    m_Localized: "My birthday passed, we didn\u2019t go to the carnival, and we had
      to go back to the Netherlands."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27521448053968896
    m_Localized: "But suddenly, a new important site potentially containing a legendary
      Kris was found and Mama had to work past the project\u2019s supposed end date."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27521418584788992
    m_Localized: "I patiently waited every day. Her excavation hours were long and
      I was so bored at Grandma\u2019s house. The carnival on my birthday was the
      only thing I was looking forward to."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27588052347392000
    m_Localized: Next
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27588092256194560
